  "summary_en": "A Japanese journal essay by a Nanzan University philosopher in the Journal of the Robotics Society of Japan on ethics for present-day robotics. It covers ELSI and the gap between social acceptance and ethical acceptability. It also discusses Responsible Research and Innovation (RRI) and inclusiveness, the SDGs and transdisciplinary work, critiques of technofixes, and well-being as framed by IEEE Ethically Aligned Design.",
